  "requiresConcentration": true,
  "footnote": "All major courses require letter grades of C- or better. The core totals 26-27 credits: 11 Physics, 12 Math, and 3-4 Astronomy. To declare, complete at least two Physics and two Math core courses with a minimum 2.7 GPA, meet the DUS in the fourth semester, and declare a concentration. Astrophysics students may not double major in Physics. Optional honors requires a 3.5+ ASTRO GPA over the last four semesters and A- or higher in key advanced courses: ASTRO 4410 and ASTRO 4431, 4432, 4433, 4434 for Astrophysics; ASTRO 4410 and ASTRO 3301, 3302, 3303 for General Astronomy. Honors and declaration GPA rules require manual review. The catalog attaches footnote 1 to AEP 4200 even though that footnote discusses ASTRO 4410; confirm its intent with the DUS."
}
